{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"05ef6108-1d6b-4c42-90bb-15d42e852fb7","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The intended black-box behavior for the failing test case [`MapperCopyTest.testCopyWith`](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jacksonxml_5_group_c_arch/src/test/java/com/fasterxml/jackson/dataformat/xml/MapperCopyTest.java#L74-L91) has been deduced and documented in [requirement.feature](file:///Users/nothing/prometheus_workdir_microstudy/jacksonxml_5_group_c_arch/requirement.feature).\n\n### Summary of the Living Requirement\n* **Feature:** XML mapper copy configuration\n* **Scenario:** When an XML mapper is copied and configured to disable annotations, serializing an annotated object with both the original mapper and the copied mapper must produce independent root element names. Specifically, the original mapper serializes with the annotated root element name (`AnnotatedName`), while the copied mapper serializes using the default class name (`Pojo282`) and does not inherit or reuse the annotated name.\n","duration_seconds":87.414281,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":178075,"output_tokens":8986,"thinking_tokens":6759,"cache_read_tokens":508516,"total_tokens":187061}}}
